[["NSE vs BSE (simulated): the same share on India's two exchanges, minute by minute. If you already hold a share, sell it where it's dearer and buy the same number back where it's cheaper; your holding is unchanged and you keep the gap, minus costs. No orders are placed."], ["Costs for a Rs 1,00,000 trade: holdings route (sell from demat, buy back, STT both sides) 0.239%; intraday route (only if your broker lets the legs offset) 0.083%. A gap smaller than that loses money. Trade size: Rs 1,00,000 or what traded on each exchange that minute, whichever is smaller. Profits are an upper bound: the last trade of a minute may no longer be available."], [], ["Two measures: 'same minute' trades at the prices of the minute the gap shows (impossible by hand: the gap is usually two last trades up to a minute apart, and firms next to the exchange take it in milliseconds); 'next minute' places both orders in the following minute and gets that minute's prices, which is what someone watching a screen could do."], ["BY DAY", "Date", "Shares compared", "Minutes compared", "Median gap (%)", "Minutes above holdings cost", "Holdings: gaps", "Holdings: same minute (Rs)", "Holdings: next minute (Rs)", "Holdings: next-minute wins", "Intraday: gaps", "Intraday: same minute (Rs)", "Intraday: next minute (Rs)", "Intraday: next-minute wins"], ["", "'2026-11-19", 493, 118614, 0.0417, 608, 592, 52322.23, -49542.2, 12, 15389, 338205.55, -372758.08, 1042], ["", "'2026-11-18", 493, 115860, 0.0416, 665, 651, 50963.07, -47757.01, 9, 15515, 333133.35, -351932.95, 1032], ["", "'2026-11-17", 493, 117300, 0.0396, 629, 595, 38388.57, -45259.51, 13, 14983, 309385.53, -347263.87, 1057], ["", "'2026-11-16", 493, 121005, 0.0408, 758, 720, 50892.53, -50587.71, 10, 16201, 362107.66, -392446.03, 1106], ["", "'2026-11-13", 493, 118413, 0.0406, 664, 651, 46828.69, -52119.19, 7, 15195, 333949.9, -350826.16, 981], ["", "'2026-11-12", 493, 124336, 0.0399, 668, 647, 52333.82, -42947.41, 11, 15633, 348284.86, -390758